es together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><div>Coming soon: The Tracker card on a car says &quot;Coming soon&quot;: live location, the remote immobilize request and mileage from the tracker need the tracker company&#39;s connection first.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the pipeline&#39;s progress.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pipeline shows each step done, such as photo sizes, copy draft and backgrounds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">On each public photo press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>. The editor opens.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The editor suggests a box over the plate. Check it. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-out and check-in photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner, documents, tracker</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing', 'chapter', 'partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand', 'Each insurance company pays an agreed rate a day for a replacement car, by car class. The rate sheet keeps those rates with their history; a rental billed to an insurer takes its rate from it, the insurer''s invoice follows it, and each insurer''s page shows what it was billed, paid and still owes.

## The rate sheet

Open **Money** > **Insurer rates**.

1. One row for each insurer, one column for each car class (the list in Settings > Vehicle classes). Each cell shows the rate today and, under it, a rate already saved for a later date. On a phone each insurer is a card with its classes.
2. Press **Set** (or **Change**) in a cell. Type the Daily rate and, when the insurer has them, a weekly cap, a cap for 30 days, a delivery and pickup allowance, the kilometres a day and a taxes note (printed on its invoices). Choose From, say why it changed, and press **Save the rate**.
3. A change never overwrites the rate before it: it is a new rate from its date, and the earlier one stays in the history. **End** stops a rate from a date.
4. Add an insurer, or change its billing contact and email, in Settings > Insurers.

> Good to know: A car takes the rate of its pricing class; when the insurer has no rate for that class, the rate of the car''s other classes, in the order of the list. A 2024 Jetta (standard, also a sedan) replaced for an insurer that pays $65 a day for sedans is billed $65 a day.

## The rate on a rental

- Add a rental, Insurance replacement (or Insurer billed later): once the price is checked and the insurer chosen, the daily rate authorized is filled from its rate sheet for the car, with the caps and the taxes note under it.
- A different rate: type it, and Differs from the rate sheet asks for the reason. The rental is not added without it. Empty the field to take the sheet''s rate again.
- The review screen of a request or an offer does the same when you choose Bill to and the insurer: the rate follows the insurer chosen, and a rate typed that differs needs the reason.
- An insurer with no rate for the car: type the rate the adjuster authorized, as before.
- The booking''s Insurance replacement card (Overview and Money tabs) shows the insurer and the claim, the daily rate and where it comes from, Differs with the reason when it is not the sheet''s, the caps, the days covered, what the insurer pays and its invoices.

## Charges to the insurer

VLF (vehicle licence fee), LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC and Waiver Saver are charged to the insurer, a rate a day each, only on a rental billed to an insurer. They have no set price: type the rate the insurer authorized on each booking.

1. Add a rental, Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): under the insurer''s details, **Charges to the insurer** has a box for each, the rate a day before HST. Under each box the amount for the days shows; the check of the price adds each line with its HST. Leave a box empty for none.
2. A request or an offer: on the review screen, once Bill to is an insurer, the same boxes are under the insurer''s details. Save, Send offer or the updated offer keeps them; Bill to back to Renter removes them in the same save.
3. A confirmed booking: the Insurance replacement card lists each charge with its rate a day, the days and the amount. **Change the charges** (or **Add a charge**), type the rates, and press **Save the charges**. Each change is in the booking''s history and the changes to the fees.
4. Each line is the rate times the rental days, plus HST: when the dates change, the amount follows. The insurer pays them whether it pays everything or the rental only.

> Good to know: They never show for a rental the renter pays, and the database refuses them there. They print on both agreements: on Blind Spot''s, VLF in box 43, LDW in 45, T&LDW in 46, PAP/PEC in 47 (each with its rate a day and amount) and Waiver Saver in its box beside Accepted; a box with no charge says N/A.

## Invoices to the insurer

- **Draft insurer invoice** on the booking bills the insurer at the booking''s daily rate (the sheet''s, or the one typed with its reason) for the days authorized.
- The weekly cap and the cap for 30 days lower the amount of a long rental. Billed for the rental only, the insurer also pays delivery and pickup up to its allowance; billed for everything, delivery and pickup above the allowance are the renter''s.
- Each charge to the insurer is a line of its own on the invoice (for example VLF (vehicle licence fee): 3 days at $5.00 a day).
- The invoice line says the rate and where it comes from (for example at $65.00 a day, Example Mutual rate sheet, Sedan), and the PDF prints the taxes note. Send it and record its payments in Money > Insurer invoices, as before.

## Billing history

**Money** > **Insurer rates**, then the insurer''s name.

1. The tiles: bookings, days used and authorized, billed, paid, outstanding, the average daily rate and the days the insurer takes to pay (from sent to paid).
2. Rates by class (Set, Change and End work here too), then the History of the rates: each rate with its dates, its status, why it changed and who saved it.
3. Billing by class: for each class the bookings, days authorized and used, billed, paid, outstanding, the average rate and the days to pay.
4. Bookings: each booking with its class, claim, dates, days, rate (Sheet and the reason when it differs), what was billed, paid and outstanding, and its invoices (each opens its PDF).
5. Choose Picked up from and to and press **Show** for a period. **Download CSV** saves the bookings of the period for a spreadsheet.

## Emails as Blind Spot Car Rental

Insurance emails go from **Blind Spot Car Rental <blindspotcarrental@carmacars.ca>** and replies come back to that address: the insurer invoice, **Email the adjuster**, and Email the renter when you choose Blind Spot Car Rental as the sender on a booking an insurer pays. Every other email still goes from CarmaCars.

> Good to know: The address sends today. To receive the replies, the mailbox (or an alias of rent@carmacars.ca in Google Workspace) must exist.

### VLF (vehicle licensing fee)
A default VLF a day can be set in **Settings** (Insurer-billed rentals: VLF a day; $0 means none). When a rental is first billed to an insurer, that VLF is put on it as one of its charges to the insurer; change the rate or remove it there, like the others. Before the renter pays again, remove the charges to the insurer.', 'Insurance replacements: rates and billing', 'The rate sheet by insurer and car class, the rate on a rental, the invoices and the billing history.',
  'Each insurance company pays an agreed rate a day for a replacement car, by car class. The rate sheet keeps those rates with their history; a rental billed to an insurer takes its rate from it, the insurer''s invoice follows it, and each insurer''s page shows what it was billed, paid and still owes.

## The rate sheet

Open **Money** > **Insurer rates**.

1. One row for each insurer, one column for each car class (the list in Settings > Vehicle classes). Each cell shows the rate today and, under it, a rate already saved for a later date. On a phone each insurer is a card with its classes.
2. Press **Set** (or **Change**) in a cell. Type the Daily rate and, when the insurer has them, a weekly cap, a cap for 30 days, a delivery and pickup allowance, the kilometres a day and a taxes note (printed on its invoices). Choose From, say why it changed, and press **Save the rate**.
3. A change never overwrites the rate before it: it is a new rate from its date, and the earlier one stays in the history. **End** stops a rate from a date.
4. Add an insurer, or change its billing contact and email, in Settings > Insurers.

> Good to know: A car takes the rate of its pricing class; when the insurer has no rate for that class, the rate of the car''s other classes, in the order of the list. A 2024 Jetta (standard, also a sedan) replaced for an insurer that pays $65 a day for sedans is billed $65 a day.

## The rate on a rental

- Add a rental, Insurance replacement (or Insurer billed later): once the price is checked and the insurer chosen, the daily rate authorized is filled from its rate sheet for the car, with the caps and the taxes note under it.
- A different rate: type it, and Differs from the rate sheet asks for the reason. The rental is not added without it. Empty the field to take the sheet''s rate again.
- The review screen of a request or an offer does the same when you choose Bill to and the insurer: the rate follows the insurer chosen, and a rate typed that differs needs the reason.
- An insurer with no rate for the car: type the rate the adjuster authorized, as before.
- The booking''s Insurance replacement card (Overview and Money tabs) shows the insurer and the claim, the daily rate and where it comes from, Differs with the reason when it is not the sheet''s, the caps, the days covered, what the insurer pays and its invoices.

## Charges to the insurer

VLF (vehicle licence fee), LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC and Waiver Saver are charged to the insurer, a rate a day each, only on a rental billed to an insurer. They have no set price: type the rate the insurer authorized on each booking.

1. Add a rental, Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): under the insurer''s details, **Charges to the insurer** has a box for each, the rate a day before HST. Under each box the amount for the days shows; the check of the price adds each line with its HST. Leave a box empty for none.
2. A request or an offer: on the review screen, once Bill to is an insurer, the same boxes are under the insurer''s details. Save, Send offer or the updated offer keeps them; Bill to back to Renter removes them in the same save.
3. A confirmed booking: the Insurance replacement card lists each charge with its rate a day, the days and the amount. **Change the charges** (or **Add a charge**), type the rates, and press **Save the charges**. Each change is in the booking''s history and the changes to the fees.
4. Each line is the rate times the rental days, plus HST: when the dates change, the amount follows. The insurer pays them whether it pays everything or the rental only.

> Good to know: They never show for a rental the renter pays, and the database refuses them there. They print on both agreements: on Blind Spot''s, VLF in box 43, LDW in 45, T&LDW in 46, PAP/PEC in 47 (each with its rate a day and amount) and Waiver Saver in its box beside Accepted; a box with no charge says N/A.

## Invoices to the insurer

- **Draft insurer invoice** on the booking bills the insurer at the booking''s daily rate (the sheet''s, or the one typed with its reason) for the days authorized.
- The weekly cap and the cap for 30 days lower the amount of a long rental. Billed for the rental only, the insurer also pays delivery and pickup up to its allowance; billed for everything, delivery and pickup above the allowance are the renter''s.
- Each charge to the insurer is a line of its own on the invoice (for example VLF (vehicle licence fee): 3 days at $5.00 a day).
- The invoice line says the rate and where it comes from (for example at $65.00 a day, Example Mutual rate sheet, Sedan), and the PDF prints the taxes note. Send it and record its payments in Money > Insurer invoices, as before.

## Billing history

**Money** > **Insurer rates**, then the insurer''s name.

1. The tiles: bookings, days used and authorized, billed, paid, outstanding, the average daily rate and the days the insurer takes to pay (from sent to paid).
2. Rates by class (Set, Change and End work here too), then the History of the rates: each rate with its dates, its status, why it changed and who saved it.
3. Billing by class: for each class the bookings, days authorized and used, billed, paid, outstanding, the average rate and the days to pay.
4. Bookings: each booking with its class, claim, dates, days, rate (Sheet and the reason when it differs), what was billed, paid and outstanding, and its invoices (each opens its PDF).
5. Choose Picked up from and to and press **Show** for a period. **Download CSV** saves the bookings of the period for a spreadsheet.

## Emails as Blind Spot Car Rental

Insurance emails go from **Blind Spot Car Rental <blindspotcarrental@carmacars.ca>** and replies come back to that address: the insurer invoice, **Email the adjuster**, and Email the renter when you choose Blind Spot Car Rental as the sender on a booking an insurer pays. Every other email still goes from CarmaCars.

> Good to know: The address sends today. To receive the replies, the mailbox (or an alias of rent@carmacars.ca in Google Workspace) must exist.

### VLF (vehicle licensing fee)
A default VLF a day can be set in **Settings** (Insurer-billed rentals: VLF a day; $0 means none). When a rental is first billed to an insurer, that VLF is put on it as one of its charges to the insurer; change the rate or remove it there, like the others. Before the renter pays again, remove the charges to the insurer.

### Adjusters
Each insurer has its adjusters, and an invoice goes to the booking''s adjuster (else the insurer''s billing email, which is now optional).

1. On a booking, in **Insurance claim and adjuster**, press **Edit**. Choose the insurer, or **Not listed: add it** and type its name.
2. Choose a saved **Adjuster** of that insurer, or **Add the adjuster** and type the name, phone and email. A new adjuster is saved with the insurer for the next booking.
3. On **Add a rental**, **Saved adjuster** fills the adjuster''s fields; a new one typed is saved the same way (matched by email, else by name).
4. On **Insurer rates**, open an insurer: Adjusters lists them (**Add an adjuster**, **Change**).

### What was billed
**Insurer rates** shows **Billed by insurer and class**: bookings, days, the average daily rate, the rental, the charges (VLF, LDW and the others), HST and the insurer''s total. Open an insurer for **Charged by class**, **Billing by car** and **Billing by adjuster**, and each booking with its car, adjuster and charges.
',
