e="left:10.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.4%;top:89.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner&#39;s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner&#39;s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no mandate gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner statements</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Build all for a month</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Build one</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open each draft. Check it, <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> after a correction, <b class="gd-ui">Preview PDF</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Issue to the owner</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Reissue</b> sends a corrected copy; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> exports it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/400"><img src="/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:79.9%;top:27.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg" alt="An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-staff-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff commissions</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff commissions</b>. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Not earned yet</span><em>The rental is ahead, or not paid in full</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pending approval</span><em>Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>You approved it; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded the payment; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Reversed</span><em>Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">By person shows each staff member&#39;s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Prices to review</b> lists prices typed by hand; <b class="gd-ui">Sourcing claims</b> lists staff who say they sourced a website request; <b class="gd-ui">Payments made</b> lists each payment.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month&#39;s rentals</td></tr><tr><td>Customer service, finance, fleet, field staff</td><td>10% (also the field referral fee)</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off</td></tr><tr><td>On the owner statement</td><td>An owner&#39;s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner&#39;s car: from CarmaCars&#39; commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month&#39;s Sales tier) goes on the owner&#39;s next statement as an adjustment line.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-field-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Field pay</b>. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Clocked in and out</span><em>Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pay run started</span><em>Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>The figures are frozen, the period&#39;s hours are locked, the statements are numbered</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tab <b class="gd-ui">Pay run</b> shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings &gt; Program, Field pay). <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After the period ends, press <b class="gd-ui">Start the pay run</b>: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). <b class="gd-ui">Refresh the figures</b> takes in a change made since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The period&#39;s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (<b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> repeats it). The statement&#39;s number opens its PDF; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> gives the run for your accountant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> lists everyone&#39;s shifts of the period. <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hourly rates</b> shows each person&#39;s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with <b class="gd-ui">Set the rate</b> (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Field pay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overtime</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Vacation pay</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement</td></tr><tr><td>Deductions</td><td>None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer&#39;s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions that net to nothing</td><td>A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company statements</h2><p class="gd-p">CarmaCars&#39; own monthly statement, in twelve sections.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Download <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b>, <b class="gd-ui">PDF by owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">PDF by vehicle</b>, or press <b class="gd-ui">Email me the PDFs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Finalize</b> freezes the month. <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> works until then.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/reports</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:28%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.4%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.1%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.9%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from the revenue statement</h3><p class="gd-p">On an owner&#39;s page, the <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b> button sets <b class="gd-ui">How fees are paid</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Take from revenue statement</b>. Taken from the statement, the owner&#39;s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;. Approved, the invoice reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task <b class="gd-ui">Invoice ... back to the bank debit</b>.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The flat-rate agreements</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b> instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner&#39;s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK</b> is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-how-it-s-paid-bank-debit-or-deducted-from-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How it&#39;s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit on the 15th</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> (taken from the owner&#39;s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On an invoice, <b class="gd-ui">How it&#39;s paid</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For the first and last month, choose <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> on the Terms tab (or at approval).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the Terms tab, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the agreed one-off fees</b> makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner&#39;s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
-- GUIDES 0240 END
